From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:34:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild a text control when its ::placeholder look changes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Box construction resolves a shown placeholder's ::placeholder style and
copies its colour and font style onto the text input. Stylo's damage
diffs only the control's own style, so a restyle that changed just the
pseudo left the copy stale: `.invalid::placeholder { color: red }` with
the class toggled by script, or an attr() that only the pseudo reads,
kept the old colour until something else rebuilt the box.

After a control showing its placeholder is restyled, the traversal now
resolves ::placeholder again and asks for box construction when the
colour or font style differs from what construction stored.

beep-boop-🤖
---
